# Source coverage and implementation status

The catalogue maps every entry in the reviewed GOV.UK component index, NHS component and pattern indexes, and Publishing Design Guide. It includes nested publishing-template variants and the NHS review-date entry that is now withdrawn. Coverage means there is local guidance and an example or an explicit replacement; it does not mean every pattern has been installed in native Home Assistant.

## Read the status correctly

| Status | What it establishes | What it does not establish |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Maintained theme or companion | Named implementation in this repository, with stated compatibility and checks | Universal support for every Home Assistant card |
| Reference component or pattern | An authored, inspectable design with usage and testing guidance | A connected backend, device action or native HA replacement |
| Withdrawn source | A recorded source decision and a recommended replacement | A recommendation to build the obsolete component |

A working documentation control proves its local example behaviour. A live Home Assistant claim requires separate installation and route verification. The examples deliberately use invented data and local actions.

## Source inventories

| Source | Reviewed entries | Local organisation |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| [GOV.UK components](https://design-system.service.gov.uk/components/) | 37 | Shared atomic components, with civica.uk header and footer replacements |
| [NHS components](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/components) | 38 | Forms, content presentation and navigation; cards and action links share existing guidance |
| [NHS patterns](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/patterns) | 13 | Inclusive content, household tasks and page patterns |
| [Publishing Design Guide](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/) | 42 | 11 components, 1 search-filter pattern and 30 page-template entries, including nested variants |

Overlapping source entries share one canonical local page rather than creating competing implementations. The source counts therefore do not add up to a unique-page count. ONS charts, the MOJ notification badge and existing DWP/Home Office-informed guidance remain in their established sections.

The machine-readable [coverage record](../reference/coverage.json) includes every source URL, local route and example ID. The [complete sitemap](../sitemap.html) and [search](../search.html) use the same Middleman page catalogue as section navigation.

## Adaptation decisions

NHS identity rules, clinical urgency and NHS-number collection are not copied into a household application. We use civica.uk artwork, describe household consequences directly and adapt the identifier pattern to useful device and configuration identifiers. The [BSL pattern](../patterns/british-sign-language.html) makes signed-content availability, production and review requirements explicit; it does not invent a verified household video.

Publishing ministerial, organisation, statistical and policy templates become household owners, guides, reports and collections. They retain useful editorial structure while omitting government authority claims. Some patterns describe a future authored application; do not infer that a native dashboard now includes a publishing backend.

